  "worked_solution": "To calculate the $x$-intercepts, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+18x+6y & =24 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2\\cdot {0}^{2}+18x+6\\cdot 0 & =24 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+18x & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}+6x & =8 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+6x+9)-9 & =8 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}-9 & =8 \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =17 \\\\ x+3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{17} \\\\ x & =-3\\pm \\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are\n\n$$\nA(-3-\\sqrt{17},0)\\,\\text{and}\\,B(-3+\\sqrt{17},0).\n$$",
